Runloop Debian Notes
====================

- The daemon runs as the `runloop` system user and stores state under
  `/var/lib/runloop`. Logs default to `/var/log/runloop`.
- Runtime sockets and pid files live in `/run/runloop`; the CLI (`rlp`) and
  `runloopd` discover the socket according to the precedence documented in
  `/usr/share/doc/runloop/README.md`.
- Default configuration is shipped at `/etc/runloop/config.yaml`. Adjust model
  routes, KB locations, or observability endpoints there and restart the daemon:

      sudo systemctl restart runloopd

- Use the `rlp` CLI (installed with the package) to run openings or inspect
  configuration layers. All binaries respect the same config file/environment
  overrides.

- During upgrades the maintainer scripts preserve local state. Purging the
  package removes `/etc/runloop`, `/var/lib/runloop`, and the `runloop` system
  user.
